---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy — SanMu Audio"
  description="SanMu Audio privacy policy: site visits, email feedback and data handling."
>
  <Nav lang="en" />

  <header class="page-hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow t-eyebrow reveal"><span class="dot"></span>SANMU AUDIO · LEGAL</div>
    <h1 class="t-display reveal">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="hero-prop reveal">Effective October 2026</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="wrap legal" style="padding-top:32px;">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p class="t-meta">SanMu Audio (“we”) respects your privacy. This policy explains how the site currently handles visit statistics and information that you choose to send us.</p>

        <h3>1. What we collect today</h3>
        <p class="t-meta">If you contact us by email, we receive the email address, name, project context and message that you choose to provide. The product-page comment feature is enabled only after the production database is configured; when enabled, it may store the email, comment, vote and moderation state that you submit for product feedback. Plug-in downloads and payments are still not open.</p>

        <h3>2. How we use it</h3>
        <p class="t-meta">Email information is used to answer questions, handle product feedback, investigate compatibility and discuss partnerships. We do not sell your email to advertisers or use message content for unrelated marketing.</p>

        <h3>3. Visit statistics</h3>
        <p class="t-meta">If Umami is configured for the site, it is used to count page visits. The deployment configuration determines whether analytics is enabled; the site does not intentionally set advertising-tracking cookies.</p>

        <h3>4. Retention and deletion</h3>
        <p class="t-meta">Emails are retained for the time needed to complete the conversation and relevant product follow-up. You can email contact@sanmuaudio.com to request deletion of related contact records, and we will process the request within a reasonable period.</p>

        <h3>5. Policy updates</h3>
        <p class="t-meta">When downloads, payments, licensing or account features open, this policy will be updated first to explain the new data, purpose, retention and deletion practices.</p>

        <h3>6. Contact</h3>
        <p class="t-meta">For privacy questions, email contact@sanmuaudio.com.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer lang="en" />
</Base>
